   "file": "lessons/week-00-orientation.md",
   "body": "# Week 0 — Orientation (Day 0, ~4 hours)\n\nComplete this before Week 1. It costs you half a day and saves you weeks.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Why this matters\n\nMost people who try to enter tender writing fail for administrative reasons, not intellectual ones: no filing system, no source discipline, no record of what they have learned, and an AI habit of generating confident fiction. You are fixing all four today.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Learning objectives\n\nBy the end of Day 0 you can:\n- Navigate the eTenders portal and download a complete tender pack unaided.\n- Explain the difference between an enacted Act and a commenced Act.\n- State the five AI ground rules from memory.\n- Show a working folder structure and a tender log with its first row.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Core concepts\n\n### 3.1 Enacted vs commenced\nAn Act can be signed and published and still have **no legal force** until a commencement date is proclaimed. The Public Procurement Act 28 of 2024 is in exactly this state. Draft regulations under it are *drafts* — useful for anticipating direction, worthless as authority.\n\n**Practical consequence:** for the next 90 days your authority stack is, in order:\n1. The tender document itself (including corrigenda and clarification notes)\n2. PFMA or MFMA, depending on the organ of state\n3. PPPFA + Preferential Procurement Regulations 2022\n4. CIDB prescripts (for construction)\n5. Sector legislation (COIDA, NHBRC, OHSA, PSIRA, etc.)\n6. Treasury instruction notes and practice notes\n\n### 3.2 National/provincial vs municipal\n- **National & provincial** organs of state → PFMA → **SBD** forms.\n- **Municipalities & municipal entities** → MFMA → **MBD** forms.\n\nThis single distinction predicts which forms appear in a pack. Learn to identify the buyer type in the first 60 seconds.\n\n### 3.3 The source-reference habit\nEvery statement you ever make about a tender carries a reference: *\"Mandatory — Volume 1, clause 4.2.3, page 17.\"* If you cannot cite it, you do not yet know it. This habit is the entire difference between a specialist and a guesser.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Setup tasks\n\n1. **Accounts:** register on eTenders (free) and bookmark the opportunity search with filters saved for your provinces.\n2. **Folder structure** — create locally and mirror in this workspace:\n   ```\n   tenders/\n     <BuyerAcronym>-<TenderNo>-<ShortTitle>/\n       00-source-pack/      (original PDFs, unmodified, read-only)\n       01-corrigenda/\n       02-analysis/         (matrix, eligibility check, go-no-go)\n       03-drafts/           (methodology, CVs, experience sheets)\n       04-client-inputs/\n       05-final-submission/\n       notes.md\n   ```\n   **Rule:** files in `00-source-pack` are never edited. Ever.\n3. **Tender log:** open `worklog/tender-log.csv` and keep it updated after every pack.\n4. **Tender Bible:** open `TENDER-BIBLE.md`. Add at least one entry every single study day.\n5. **AI workspace:** create a project named *SA Tender Academy*, paste the five ground rules as permanent instructions, and create the seven working chats.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Practical assignment (Day 0)\n\n- Download **one** real tender pack of any kind from eTenders. Complete, including annexures.\n- Skim it once for 20 minutes only. Write half a page answering just two questions:\n  - What would make this bidder lose before anyone reads their proposal?\n  - What would make them score badly even if fully compliant?\n- Do not research. Do not use AI. This is a baseline snapshot of your current ability — you will repeat this exact exercise in Week 12 and compare.\n\nSave as `worklog/baseline-day0.md`.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Self-test\n\n1. Which Act governs a metropolitan municipality's procurement, and which bid-document family will it use?\n2. Why can you not cite the Public Procurement Act 28 of 2024 as the operative framework today?\n3. What are the five layers of tender analysis?\n4. What is the one folder you never edit?\n\n---\n\n## 7. AI drill prompt\n\n> You are my procurement tutor. Do not explain anything yet. Ask me 10 questions to test whether I understand the difference between national/provincial and municipal procurement frameworks in South Africa, the current status of the Public Procurement Act 28 of 2024, and the five-layer tender analysis model. Grade each answer, correct every mistake, and cite the official source for each correction.\n\n---\n\n## 8. Mastery gate\n\n✅ Folder structure exists · ✅ eTenders account working · ✅ one full pack downloaded · ✅ baseline note written · ✅ five ground rules recited from memory.\n",
