   "id": "tender-bible",
   "kind": "guide",
   "label": "The Tender Bible",
   "sub": "Your knowledge asset",
   "title": "The Tender Bible",
   "file": "TENDER-BIBLE.md",
   "body": "# The Tender Bible\n\nYour operating system. Add at least one entry every study day. After 90 days this is your most valuable asset — more valuable than any single client.\n\n**Rule:** every entry carries a source and the date you verified it. Regulations, forms, thresholds and CIDB limits change.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Definitions (Week 1)\n\nDefine each term by its **effect on a bid**, not its dictionary meaning.\n\n| Term | Definition | Effect on a bid | Source | Verified |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Responsiveness | | | | |\n| Material deviation | | | | |\n| Functionality | | | | |\n| Returnable | | | | |\n| Corrigendum | | | | |\n| Bid validity period | | | | |\n| Two-envelope system | | | | |\n| Condonation | | | | |\n\n---\n\n## 2. SBD / MBD forms (Week 2)\n\n| Form | Framework | What it establishes | Who signs | Common failure | Source | Verified |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| SBD 1 | PFMA | | | | ocpo.treasury.gov.za | |\n| SBD 4 | PFMA | | | | | |\n| SBD 6.1 | PFMA | | | | | |\n| MBD equivalents | MFMA | | | | | |\n\n---\n\n## 3. Compliance documents — what each proves (Week 2 & 10)\n\n| Document | What it proves | Issuer | Lead time | Validity/expiry | Trigger (when required) | Source | Verified |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| CSD registration | | CSD | | rolling | | | |\n| SARS Tax Compliance Status (Good Standing PIN) | | SARS | | live status | | | |\n| B-BBEE affidavit / certificate | | Commissioner / SANAS agency | | | | | |\n| CIDB registration | | CIDB | | | construction | | |\n| COIDA Letter of Good Standing | | Compensation Fund | | | | | |\n| NHBRC | | NHBRC | | annual | home building | | |\n| PSIRA | | PSIRA | | | security element | | |\n| Insurances | | Insurer | | | per contract data | | |\n\n---\n\n## 4. Evaluation terminology (Week 3)\n\n| Term | Meaning | Where it appears | Notes |\n|---|---|---|---|\n\n---\n\n## 5. Preference rules (Week 3)\n\n- Systems: **80/20** at or below **R50 million**; **90/10** above. *(Source: PPR 2022 — verify date: ____)*\n- Specific goals are set by the **procuring institution** in the tender.\n- Preference points must be **claimed and substantiated**.\n- Pre-qualification is a **gate**, not points.\n\nWorked calculation examples:\n\n| Scenario | Bid prices | Preference claims | Points | Winner | My workings correct? |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n\n---\n\n## 6. CIDB grades, classes and limits (Weeks 5–6)\n\n**Guide version used:** ____________  **Date verified:** ____________\n\n| Grade | Tender value limit |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | |\n| 2 | R1m |\n| 3 | R3m |\n| 4 | R6m |\n| 5 | R10m |\n| 6 | R20m |\n| 7 | R60m |\n| 8 | R200m |\n| 9 | Unlimited |\n\n| Class | Meaning | Typical work |\n|---|---|---|\n| GB | General Building | |\n| CE | Civil Engineering | |\n| EB | Electrical Engineering Works – Building | |\n| EP | Electrical Engineering Works – Infrastructure | |\n| ME | Mechanical Engineering | |\n| Specialist classes | | |\n\n**Status notes:** active · suspended/lapsed · potentially emerging · upgrades · JV calculation · track record.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Construction terminology (Week 7)\n\n| Term | Concept | Why it matters to a bid |\n|---|---|---|\n| BOQ | | |\n| Preliminaries | | |\n| Provisional sum | | |\n| Prime cost sum | | |\n| Retention | | |\n| Performance guarantee | | |\n| Practical completion | | |\n| Defects liability period | | |\n| Variation | | |\n| Extension of time | | |\n| Liquidated damages | | |\n| Contract data | | |\n\n---\n\n## 8. Template library index\n\n| Template | File | Last improved |\n|---|---|---|\n| Compliance matrix | templates/compliance-matrix.csv | |\n| Tender intake checklist | templates/tender-intake-checklist.md | |\n| Eligibility determination | templates/eligibility-determination.md | |\n| Go/no-go checklist | templates/go-no-go-checklist.md | |\n| Method statement | templates/method-statement.md | |\n| Risk register | templates/risk-register.csv | |\n| CV template | templates/cv-template.md | |\n| Experience schedule | templates/experience-sheet.md | |\n| Red-team checklist | templates/red-team-checklist.md | |\n| Submission checklist | templates/submission-checklist.md | |\n\n---\n\n## 9. Banned filler phrases\n\nPhrases I have caught myself writing that communicate nothing:\n\n- \"highly experienced team\"\n- \"committed to excellence\"\n- \"customer satisfaction\"\n- \"world-class service\"\n- \"we understand the importance of…\"\n- \n\n---\n\n## 10. Errors I have personally made\n\nThe most valuable section in this document. One line per error, forever.\n\n| Date | Tender | Error | Consequence | Rule I now follow |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n\n---\n\n## 11. Regulatory watch list\n\n| Item | Status | Last checked | Source |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Public Procurement Act 28 of 2024 commencement | Enacted; commencement to be proclaimed | | gov.za |\n| Draft General Public Procurement Regulations (2026) | Draft | | treasury.gov.za |\n| Preferential Procurement Regulations 2022 | In force | | treasury.gov.za |\n| CIDB value limits | | | cidb.org.za |\n| SBD/MBD form versions | | | ocpo.treasury.gov.za |\n",
